### ============================================================================
### REST API LEARNING LAB - MANUAL REQUESTS
### You can run these with VS Code REST Client extension, Postman, or curl!
### ============================================================================

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. GOLANG BACKEND (PORT 8080)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Golang: Health Check (Public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health
Accept: application/json

### Golang: Register a New User (Public)
# Notice we send JSON payload. Password will be hashed using bcrypt on the server!
POST http://localhost:8080/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Developer",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "securePassword456"
}

### Golang: Login with Seeded Demo Account (Public)
# Returns a signed JSON Web Token (JWT) valid for 24 hours
POST http://localhost:8080/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Golang: Attempt accessing subscriptions WITHOUT Token (Should Fail with 401)
# Demonstrates how the AuthMiddleware blocks unauthorized visitors
GET http://localhost:8080/api/subscriptions
Accept: application/json

### Golang: Access Protected Subscriptions WITH Bearer Token (Success 200)
# Replace <YOUR_TOKEN_HERE> with the token from the login response
GET http://localhost:8080/api/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_TOKEN_HERE>
Accept: application/json


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. EXPRESS.JS BACKEND (PORT 5000)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Express: Health Check (Public)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/health
Accept: application/json

### Express: Register a New User (Public)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Developer",
  "email": "jane.express@example.com",
  "password": "securePassword456"
}

### Express: Login with Seeded Demo Account (Public)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Express: Attempt accessing subscriptions WITHOUT Token (Should Fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/subscriptions
Accept: application/json

### Express: Access Protected Subscriptions WITH Bearer Token (Success 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_TOKEN_HERE>
Accept: application/json
